      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lukeville%2C_Arizona"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Lukeville sits directly on the U.S.–Mexico border opposite Sonoyta, Sonora, and hosts the Lukeville Port of Entry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lukeville%2C_Arizona"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Lukeville lies entirely within Organ Pipe Cactus National Monument, giving it a desert landscape.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lukeville%2C_Arizona"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Customs and Border Protection facility opened in 1949 and handles vehicular and pedestrian traffic to Puerto Peñasco.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Lukeville,_Arizona"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The port operates daily from 6:00 a.m. Mountain Time, but closed temporarily in December 2023 for staff reallocation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Lukeville,_Arizona"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Lukeville is the terminus of State Route 85, a short stretch that connects to the rest of Arizona.",
